      <p class="msc-section-kicker">Bitcoin Ecosystem</p>
      <h1>What Bitcoin Infrastructure Companies Do</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">Bitcoin infrastructure companies provide technical systems that other products and organizations rely on: nodes, APIs, indexers, Lightning operations, mining systems, signing hardware, developer tools, security services, and enterprise integrations. Infrastructure should be defined by function, not reputation. A hosted node, explorer, API, wallet backend, or indexer can make Bitcoin easier to use while introducing privacy, availability, policy, and vendor dependencies. None becomes an independent consensus authority merely because many customers rely on it.</p>
      <ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Companies</li><li>Shallow</li><li>Ecosystem Overview</li><li>19 to 23 minutes</li><li>Reviewed 2026-07-27</li></ul>
